        "title": {
          "en": "The young entrepreneurs challenge"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Imagine your school festival has a Young Entrepreneurs Challenge. To win you must turn an idea into a product or service people want."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "business plan",
          "entrepreneur",
          "functional areas",
          "impact",
          "learning",
          "profit",
          "startup",
          "what each does"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "An entrepreneur starts a business, takes risks and creates products or services to meet needs.\nEntrepreneurship creates jobs, new products and economic growth for society.\nA startup is a new business built around an idea, often using new technology.\nThe functional areas of a business are production, marketing, finance and human resources.\nProduction makes the product, marketing sells it, finance manages money and human resources manages people.\nA business plan describes the idea, customers, costs, prices and expected profit.\nProfit is revenue minus costs. A business that earns less than it spends makes a loss.\nMany startups begin small and learn from failures."
        }
